Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1038
00:49:55.690 --> 00:49:56.630
You guys, wait.
你们等一下。

1039
00:49:56.710 --> 00:49:58.090
I have to put some context in this.
我得交代一下背景。

1040
00:49:58.210 --> 00:49:59.370
I have done this ride.
我坐过那个项目。

1041
00:49:59.510 --> 00:50:02.010
It has got such a huge drop.
它的下坠幅度特别大。

1042
00:50:02.450 --> 00:50:02.570
Yep.
没错。

1043
00:50:02.590 --> 00:50:04.070
I've done it with the kids.
我和孩子们一起坐过。

1044
00:50:04.230 --> 00:50:08.890
We have we bought the photo, you know, the photo when you do the drop and the kids faces.
我们买了那张照片，就是你下坠时拍的那张，孩子们的表情。

1045
00:50:09.190 --> 00:50:10.050
It's like horror.
简直是惊恐万状。

1046
00:50:10.050 --> 00:50:12.610
The drop is so much bigger than you can prepare for.
那个下坠比你预想的要大得多。

1047
00:50:12.770 --> 00:50:15.810
And I got completely soaked.
我全身都湿透了。

1048
00:50:16.050 --> 00:50:19.770
I had to go to the gift shop and I had to buy a pair of sweatpants to wear around the rest
我不得不去礼品店买了一条运动裤，好在剩下的时间里穿着，

1049
00:50:19.770 --> 00:50:21.370
of the day because I was drenched.
因为我当时全身上下都湿透了。

1050
00:50:21.650 --> 00:50:21.810
Yeah.
是啊。

1051
00:50:22.070 --> 00:50:24.870
This was my first acting job when I arrived in Los Angeles.
这是我刚到洛杉矶时接到的第一份表演工作。

1052
00:50:25.070 --> 00:50:26.730
My friend and I both signed up.
我和朋友都报名参加了。

1053
00:50:26.870 --> 00:50:27.450
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1054
00:50:27.450 --> 00:50:31.030
We were so excited when we got to Universal Studios.
我们到达环球影城时兴奋极了。

1055
00:50:31.250 --> 00:50:36.390
As we're walking in, we passed by Arnold Schwarzenegger shooting baskets outside of a sound
我们走进去的时候，路过阿诺德·施瓦辛格，他当时正在摄影棚外投篮。

1056
00:50:36.390 --> 00:50:36.650
stage.
我们当时心想，我们终于出人头地了。

1057
00:50:36.650 --> 00:50:38.590
We were like, we have arrived.
这绝对会是有史以来最棒的一天。

1058
00:50:38.590 --> 00:50:41.230
This is going to be the best day ever.
呜呼。

1059
00:50:41.470 --> 00:50:41.870
Woo hoo.
十二个小时后，你离开时哭了吗？

1060
00:50:42.470 --> 00:50:45.250
Twelve hours later, did you cry as you left?
我们去片场时和一天结束离开片场时，那感觉简直天差地别。

1061
00:50:45.730 --> 00:50:51.550
The difference of us walking to the gig and walking from the gig at the end of the day,
我们当时被折磨得精疲力竭。

1062
00:50:51.770 --> 00:50:53.210
we were so beaten down.
我想说的是，在某个时刻，他们觉得自己的出镜率不够高。

1063
00:50:53.390 --> 00:50:58.890
I want to say at a certain point, they felt like they weren't getting on camera enough
往我们身上泼水来表现这是一个水上游乐设施。

1064
00:50:58.890 --> 00:51:02.630
water splashing on us to indicate that it was a water ride.
不。

1065
00:51:02.870 --> 00:51:02.990
No.
所以他们做的第一件事就是找人提着水桶。

1066
00:51:02.990 --> 00:51:07.950
So the first thing they did was they had guys with buckets of water that they would just
当我们坐着小船滑过时，他们就直接把水泼在我们身上。

1067
00:51:07.950 --> 00:51:11.210
throw on us as we scooted by in the little boat.
噢，不。

1068
00:51:11.430 --> 00:51:11.970
Oh, no.
但后来，连这都不够了。

1069
00:51:12.310 --> 00:51:15.070
But at one point, not even that was enough.
他们拿出了所谓的“水炮”。

1070
00:51:15.230 --> 00:51:17.870
They got out what's called a water cannon.
不会吧。

1071
00:51:18.470 --> 00:51:18.730
No.
没错。

1072
00:51:19.370 --> 00:51:19.510
Yep.
天哪。

1073
00:51:19.670 --> 00:51:20.350
Oh, my gosh.
他们直接用水炮朝你轰。

1074
00:51:20.350 --> 00:51:23.490
They shoot cannonballs of water at you.
珍娜。

1075
00:51:23.830 --> 00:51:24.070
Jenna.
你敢信吗？

1076
00:51:24.590 --> 00:51:25.270
Can you believe?
我真不敢相信在那之后我居然没直接开车回密苏里州。

1077
00:51:25.290 --> 00:51:28.630
I can't believe I didn't just drive back to Missouri after that.
这就是当演员啊。

1078
00:51:30.290 --> 00:51:31.910
This is being an actor.
是啊。

1079
00:51:32.470 --> 00:51:32.630
Yeah.
十二个小时。

1080
00:51:32.970 --> 00:51:33.910
Twelve hours.
那游乐设施我坐了一次，当时就想，我再也不要坐第二次了。

1081
00:51:34.110 --> 00:51:37.510
I rode that ride one time and I was like, I'm never doing it again.
好吧，如果你看那个广告，有一个地方你可以暂停。

1082
00:51:37.510 --> 00:51:42.490
Well, if you see the commercial, there is a spot where you can pause.
在那一秒钟里，屏幕上能看到我的一半身体。

1083
00:51:42.670 --> 00:51:46.610
And for one second, half of me is on screen.
所以，这位女士，当你在克莱·沃克的音乐录影带里跳舞时，我正在被水炮轰炸。

1084
00:51:47.430 --> 00:51:52.870
So, lady, while you were dancing to this Clay Walker music video, I was getting hit by a water
这就是演艺圈，各位。

1085
00:51:52.870 --> 00:51:53.250
cannon.
天呐。

1086
00:51:53.710 --> 00:51:55.050
That's showbiz, folks.
好吧，我们休息一下，回来后从商学院开始聊。

1087
00:51:55.830 --> 00:51:56.690
Oh, man.
好的。

1088
00:51:56.990 --> 00:52:00.630
Well, let's take a break and we will come back and we'll start with business school.
我们回来了。

1089
00:52:00.870 --> 00:52:11.030
All right.
我们要从商学院开始聊。

1090
00:52:11.030 --> 00:52:12.210
We are back.
这一集是帕姆的艺术展，我们收到了很多艺术家的来信，女士。

1091
00:52:12.510 --> 00:52:13.930
We're going to start with business school.
因为这一集播出后，他们真的和帕姆产生了共鸣。

1092
00:52:13.930 --> 00:52:20.870
This is the episode with Pam's art show and we got mail, lady, from so many artists after
这一集里还有办公室进蝙蝠的情节，很多人跟我们分享了他们办公室里也进过蝙蝠的经历。

1093
00:52:20.870 --> 00:52:23.310
this episode because they really connected with Pam.
什么？

1094
00:52:23.490 --> 00:52:29.770
This is also the episode with the bat in the office and several people shared with us about
办公室里有蝙蝠？

1095
00:52:29.770 --> 00:52:31.970
having bats in their offices.
是的。

1096
00:52:32.250 --> 00:52:32.530
What?
听听这个。

1097
00:52:32.830 --> 00:52:34.430
Bats in their offices?
凯莉·拉登说，重温这一集让她回想起自己工作时的一段经历。

1098
00:52:34.830 --> 00:52:35.290
Yes.
当时我正在工作。

1099
00:52:35.430 --> 00:52:36.430
Listen to this one.
当时我正在工作。

1100
00:52:36.750 --> 00:52:42.430
Kelly Rarden said, rewatching this episode gave me flashbacks of the time I was working
当时我正在工作。

1101
00:52:42.430 --> 00:52:49.370
alone in my office late at night during a thunderstorm and a bat started swooping at my head.
深夜雷雨交加，我独自在办公室里，一只蝙蝠开始朝我头上俯冲。

1102
00:52:49.530 --> 00:52:55.070
I was on a tight deadline, so I had to dodge the bat for an hour while I tried to continue
当时我赶着截止日期，所以不得不一边躲避蝙蝠，一边尝试继续

1103
00:52:55.070 --> 00:52:55.650
working.
工作。

1104
00:52:56.130 --> 00:52:57.950
Kelly, did you get a rabies shot?
凯莉，你打狂犬疫苗了吗？

1105
00:52:58.290 --> 00:52:59.770
I hope Kelly got a rabies shot.
我希望凯莉打了狂犬疫苗。

1106
00:52:59.830 --> 00:53:02.470
Remember, you can't always feel it when they bite you.
记住，它们咬你的时候你未必能感觉到。

1107
00:53:02.650 --> 00:53:04.210
I know they're sneaky.
我知道它们很狡猾。

1108
00:53:04.210 --> 00:53:09.770
And speaking of bats, Kendra Zane said, I can't believe you guys didn't touch on the
说到蝙蝠，肯德拉·赞恩说，真不敢相信你们竟然没提到

1109
00:53:09.770 --> 00:53:11.730
rabies foreshadowing with Meredith.
梅雷迪思那段关于狂犬病的铺垫。

1110
00:53:12.010 --> 00:53:13.630
Kendra, we totally should have.
肯德拉，我们确实应该提到的。

1111
00:53:13.950 --> 00:53:14.650
Great catch.
观察得真仔细。

1112
00:53:14.850 --> 00:53:15.610
All right, Angela.
好了，安吉拉。

1113
00:53:15.810 --> 00:53:16.850
Remember cocktails?
还记得鸡尾酒会那集吗？

1114
00:53:17.350 --> 00:53:18.150
Yes, I do.
记得，当然记得。

1115
00:53:18.450 --> 00:53:20.890
Michael goes to the party at David Wallace's house.
迈克尔去了大卫·华莱士家参加聚会。

1116
00:53:21.190 --> 00:53:24.670
Do you remember the creepy ghost lady in the background of Michael's talking head?
你还记得迈克尔对着镜头说话时，背景里那个诡异的幽灵女士吗？

1117
00:53:24.830 --> 00:53:25.670
How could I forget?
我怎么可能忘得了？

1118
00:53:25.930 --> 00:53:26.510
So creepy.
太诡异了。

1119
00:53:26.850 --> 00:53:31.270
A lot of people wrote in to say they think it was someone from the catering staff.
很多人写信来说，他们认为那是餐饮服务人员之一。

1120
00:53:31.270 --> 00:53:31.910
Wow.
哇。

1121
00:53:32.130 --> 00:53:38.290
They noted that the woman is wearing the same burgundy top as the other caterers, and
他们指出那个女人穿着和其他餐饮人员一样的酒红色上衣，

1122
00:53:38.290 --> 00:53:43.590
they think she's chopping something or maybe washing dishes because her shoulders and arms
他们认为她当时可能在切东西或者洗碗，因为她的肩膀和手臂

1123
00:53:43.590 --> 00:53:44.950
are kind of moving a little bit.
在微微晃动。

1124
00:53:45.130 --> 00:53:49.070
You guys really, really gave this a once over.
你们真的把这集研究得太透彻了。

1125
00:53:49.250 --> 00:53:52.050
I mean, if you're clocking her shoulder movements, I'm impressed.
我是说，如果你们连她肩膀的动作都注意到了，我真是佩服。

1126
00:53:52.330 --> 00:53:58.410
Well, Mando said the ghost from the talking head is also in the kitchen at 6 minutes, 33 seconds
曼多说，那个对着镜头说话时的幽灵，在6分33秒时也出现在厨房里，

1127
00:53:58.410 --> 00:54:01.510
as David's wife puts down Michael's potato salad.
当时大卫的妻子放下了迈克尔带来的土豆沙拉。

1128
00:54:01.670 --> 00:54:07.370
And Leslie Heath said you can see her walk behind Michael and Jan at 14 minutes, 3 seconds.
莱斯利·希思说，在14分3秒时，你可以看到她走在迈克尔和简的身后。

1129
00:54:07.690 --> 00:54:11.150
This is so much more than I ever thought we would know about this ghost woman.
关于这个幽灵女士，我们知道的信息比我预想的要多得多。

1130
00:54:11.650 --> 00:54:13.070
I know, it's so true.
我知道，确实如此。

1131
00:54:13.650 --> 00:54:16.690
So not a ghost, member of catering staff.
所以不是幽灵，是餐饮服务人员。

1132
00:54:16.910 --> 00:54:17.310
Okay.
好吧。

1133
00:54:17.530 --> 00:54:19.570
I've got a few more catches for you.
我还有几个发现要告诉你们。

1134
00:54:19.570 --> 00:54:25.230
Charlie said, I'd like to point out that when Jan presents Michael with their love contract,
查理说，我想指出的是，当简把他们的恋爱协议交给迈克尔时，

1135
00:54:25.510 --> 00:54:27.550
Michael says, I'm going to frame mine.
迈克尔说，我要把我的那份裱起来。

1136
00:54:27.710 --> 00:54:32.450
In the later episode, The Deposition, when Jan is attempting to sue Dunder Mifflin,
在后来的《证词》那一集中，当简试图起诉邓德·米夫林公司时，

1137
00:54:32.990 --> 00:54:37.130
Michael presents the contract as evidence, and it's in a black frame.
迈克尔把那份协议作为证据提交了，而且它是装在一个黑色相框里的。

1138
00:54:37.630 --> 00:54:37.890
Nice.
不错。

1139
00:54:38.410 --> 00:54:40.250
It's so good, isn't it?
这太棒了，不是吗？

1140
00:54:40.530 --> 00:54:45.490
And Chris G says, you didn't mention the fact that Jan drove her own car to the party,
克里斯·G说，你们没提到简是自己开车去参加聚会的，

1141
00:54:45.490 --> 00:54:50.230
but then rode home with Michael, what happened to her car?
但后来是坐迈克尔的车回家的，她的车去哪了？

1142
00:54:50.470 --> 00:54:51.630
I had wondered about that.
我也一直纳闷这个问题。

1143
00:54:51.750 --> 00:54:57.470
I have to say, I wondered, did they have to drive back to David Wallace's house and pick
我得说，我当时就在想，他们是不是得开车回大卫·华莱士家去取

1144
00:54:57.470 --> 00:54:57.770
up her car?
她的车？

1145
00:54:57.850 --> 00:54:58.770
You know what I think she did?
你知道我觉得她是怎么做的吗？

1146
00:54:58.770 --> 00:55:02.210
I think she sent Michael in a cab the next day to get her car.
我觉得她第二天打发迈克尔坐出租车去把她的车取回来了。

1147
00:55:02.390 --> 00:55:04.950
I think she drank too much wine and...
我觉得她当时红酒喝多了，然后……

1148
00:55:04.950 --> 00:55:07.090
Oh, well, that's for sure why Michael drove her.
哦，那肯定就是迈克尔开车送她的原因。

1149
00:55:07.310 --> 00:55:11.190
But how she retrieved her car, I bet she made Michael go get it.
但至于她怎么取回的车，我敢打赌她肯定是让迈克尔去取的。

1150
00:55:11.330 --> 00:55:13.270
And then I bet Michael made Dwight go get it.
然后我敢打赌迈克尔又让德怀特去取的。

1151
00:55:14.310 --> 00:55:15.990
Exactly, exactly.
没错，确实如此。

1152
00:55:16.470 --> 00:55:21.410
Well, moving on to the negotiation, my pocket soapbox got a lot of mail.
好了，继续谈谈关于口袋的话题，我那个关于口袋的“肥皂箱”演讲收到了很多来信。

1153
00:55:21.590 --> 00:55:28.790
In support of my position, one of my favorites came from Melanie Vergara, who said,
为了支持我的观点，我最喜欢的一封信来自梅兰妮·维加拉，她说：

1154
00:55:29.110 --> 00:55:35.810
Ladies, I feel so strongly about the symbology of pockets that I refuse to even consider buying
女士们，我对口袋的象征意义深信不疑，以至于我拒绝考虑购买

1155
00:55:35.810 --> 00:55:37.550
a wedding dress without pockets.
任何没有口袋的婚纱。

1156
00:55:37.550 --> 00:55:40.490
And I found the wedding dress of my dreaMs.
结果我找到了我梦寐以求的婚纱。

1157
00:55:40.490 --> 00:55:41.670
It has pockets.
它有口袋。

1158
00:55:41.830 --> 00:55:43.370
She's going to wear it this year.
她今年就要穿上它了。

1159
00:55:43.570 --> 00:55:46.010
I mean, a wedding dress with pockets is pretty phenomenal.
我是说，有口袋的婚纱真是太棒了。

1160
00:55:46.270 --> 00:55:46.410
Yeah.
没错。

1161
00:55:46.870 --> 00:55:51.470
Well, Kinney, who is a historian, wrote in and had a correction for us.
还有一位叫金尼的历史学家写信来纠正我们的说法。

1162
00:55:51.790 --> 00:55:58.030
Kinney says, women had pockets throughout history until the 1800s, when for various complicated
金尼说，女性在历史上一直都有口袋，直到19世纪，由于各种复杂

1163
00:55:58.030 --> 00:56:01.510
and mostly sexist reasons, women lost their pockets.
且大多带有性别歧视的原因，女性失去了口袋。

1164
00:56:01.790 --> 00:56:04.770
So yes, the lack of pockets is a sexist thing.
所以没错，没有口袋确实是性别歧视的问题。

1165
00:56:04.770 --> 00:56:08.210
But the 400 years ago thing is wrong.
但“400年前”那个说法是错的。

1166
00:56:08.430 --> 00:56:10.010
It's more like 200.
其实大概是200年前。

1167
00:56:10.430 --> 00:56:14.190
Secondly, she says, corsets were not bad for you.
其次，她说，束身衣其实对身体没坏处。

1168
00:56:14.350 --> 00:56:16.310
In fact, they gave you great back support.
事实上，它们能提供很好的背部支撑。

1169
00:56:16.590 --> 00:56:22.010
The reason corsets hurt people today is because they either haven't broken them in the same way
现在的人穿束身衣觉得疼，要么是因为没像磨合硬质鞋子那样

1170
00:56:22.010 --> 00:56:26.270
you have to break in a stiff material shoe before they're comfortable or because they
把束身衣穿合身，要么是因为

1171
00:56:26.270 --> 00:56:27.390
are not fitted properly.
它们根本就不合身。

1172
00:56:27.390 --> 00:56:32.890
Because people today don't realize the absolute importance of a well-fitted corset and that
因为现代人没意识到一件合身的束身衣有多重要，而且

1173
00:56:32.890 --> 00:56:37.670
she would personally take a corset over a bra any day.
她个人宁愿穿束身衣也不愿穿胸罩。

1174
00:56:38.230 --> 00:56:38.470
Wow.
哇。

1175
00:56:38.830 --> 00:56:40.230
It's a lot of information there.
信息量真大。

1176
00:56:40.570 --> 00:56:42.590
Kinney, I could not love this letter more.
金尼，我太喜欢这封信了。

1177
00:56:42.810 --> 00:56:43.770
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

1178
00:56:43.930 --> 00:56:48.970
Although I do have to say, having worn many corsets for acting projects over the year,
虽然我不得不说，多年来为了演戏穿过很多次束身衣，

1179
00:56:49.070 --> 00:56:50.330
perhaps they were ill-fitted.
可能我穿的那些都不合身吧。

1180
00:56:50.570 --> 00:56:51.970
I'm going to go ahead and take a bra.
我还是选胸罩吧。

1181
00:56:52.270 --> 00:56:54.010
You're going to take a bra over a corset?
你宁愿选胸罩也不选束身衣？

1182
00:56:54.010 --> 00:56:57.410
I'm going to take a sports bra, if I'm being honeSt.
老实说，我会选运动内衣。

1183
00:56:57.710 --> 00:57:01.270
I don't even want any of the underwire if I can avoid it.
如果可以的话，我连钢圈都不想要。

1184
00:57:01.470 --> 00:57:04.190
